Sign out of the selected profile. A browser login's session is deleted on
the dashboard first (gateway tokens already issued from it stop working
within seconds), then removed from the keychain or
credentials file. An API key saved with --with-api-key is removed from the
profile (revoke the key itself in the dashboard).

Usage:
  anona-compute logout [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help    help for logout
      --local   only remove local credentials; do not contact the dashboard

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output: one object per line on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
